\newlabel{fig:theory}{{1}{4}{Evaluation theory vs.\ simulation. (a) Coverage given the calibration set ($\ell _2$ score, logistic-normal, oracle $f$; $2\times 10^4$ calibration draws per $n$) against the Beta law. (b) Probability that a valid method's one-run coverage lies more than $0.02$ from $0.9$; lines: Beta--Binomial law, dots: simulation. (c) $K{=}2$ conditional coverage vs.\ $f_1(x)$ ($\tau =1$, $n_{\rm cal}=2000$, 40 calibrations); dashed: closed form of Prop.~\ref {prop:pivot}c}{figure.caption.1}{}}
